From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nomorecoolnicknames <nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:19:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] libprocessgroup: fall back to a named v1 hierarchy when
 cgroup2 is missing

Kernels older than 4.5 have no cgroup2 filesystem. On them the mount fails
with ENODEV, /sys/fs/cgroup stays a bare sysfs directory, mkdir uid_0
returns EPERM and init cannot start any service (createProcessGroup failed
-> bootstrap-apexd-failed). The uid/pid process-group hierarchy only needs
mkdir/rmdir and cgroup.procs, which a controller-less named v1 hierarchy
provides.

Seen on the Meizu MX6 (3.18.22 kernel).

Change-Id: I467450b592aefa2ce4d0bdd3f89920c58f0c79d6

diff --git a/libprocessgroup/setup/cgroup_map_write.cpp b/libprocessgroup/setup/cgroup_map_write.cpp
index 3831ef2..3b231c0 100644
--- a/libprocessgroup/setup/cgroup_map_write.cpp
+++ b/libprocessgroup/setup/cgroup_map_write.cpp
@@ -278,6 +278,18 @@ static bool SetupCgroup(const CgroupDescriptor& descriptor) {
                 if (mount("none", controller->path(), "cgroup2", MS_NODEV | MS_NOEXEC | MS_NOSUID,
                           nullptr) < 0) {
                     PLOG(ERROR) << "Failed to mount cgroup v2";
+                    // Legacy kernels (< 4.5) have no cgroup2 filesystem. The uid/pid process
+                    // group hierarchy only needs mkdir/rmdir and cgroup.procs, which a
+                    // controller-less named v1 hierarchy provides. Without it no service can
+                    // be started (createProcessGroup fails with EPERM on the bare sysfs dir).
+                    if (errno == ENODEV &&
+                        mount("none", controller->path(), "cgroup",
+                              MS_NODEV | MS_NOEXEC | MS_NOSUID, "none,name=android_pg") < 0) {
+                        PLOG(ERROR) << "Failed to mount v1 fallback for cgroup v2";
+                    } else if (errno == ENODEV) {
+                        LOG(INFO) << "Mounted named v1 hierarchy at " << controller->path()
+                                  << " in place of cgroup v2";
+                    }
                 }
             }
 
